    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DRQMYNBXN53FKBCBKG\">How to apply brand voice guidelines to AI-generated email content</h2>\n<p>Learn how to create and apply brand voice guidelines to ensure your AI-generated email content aligns with your brand identity. This helps drive consistency and reduce editing time when using Klaviyo’s generative AI features to create email content.</p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-requirements\">\n<p>You must have a paid Klaviyo account to use this feature.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DRNEWZ8PAP318MVTS5\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>This article covers an option for customizing AI-generated email content. If you’re new to Email AI, see our <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/28242227715227\">guide on using Email AI</a>. Or, if you want to create a campaign without AI, <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005054847\">learn how to create and send an email campaign</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DRYEEJPPSKKWBBEX8Y\">What are brand voice guidelines?</h2>\n<p>Brand voice guidelines help you maintain a consistent brand identity by defining the tone and writing patterns that represent your brand. Key components of brand voice include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Voice descriptor title: Words to define your brand's communication style or personality (e.g., playful, formal, or opinionated). \n<ul>\n<li>Description: Each descriptor must include a description to convey its meaning, including examples and keywords for added detail.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Writing Rules: Rules to create clear guidelines that provide structure and help you maintain consistency in your messaging (e.g., rules for emoji usage, punctuation, or sentence length). \n<ul>\n<li>Rule application description: Rules must include indication of when and how they should be applied.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Klaviyo can automatically generate these for you, and you can customize and adjust them manually afterward. When created, brand voice guidelines for your account automatically apply to email template drafts created by Email AI. </p>\n<div class=\"accordion accordion--default\">\n<div class=\"accordion__item\">\n<div class=\"accordion__item-title\"><strong>How brand voice guidelines are generated</strong></div>\n<div class=\"accordion__item-content\">\n<p>Brand voice guidelines are generated through the following process: </p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<strong>Analysis: </strong>Klaviyo analyzes your past email content to identify your brand’s unique tone, vocabulary, and writing patterns. </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Sample generation</strong>: Samples are generated reflecting the inferred brand voice guidelines. From here, you can edit as needed to ensure alignment.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Integration</strong>: Once created, brand voice guidelines integrate into Klaviyo’s <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/28242227715227\">Email AI</a> feature, aligning all future AI-generated email content with your brand identity.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DSAS2EBPJ4ZAMRCX9E\">Configure brand voice guidelines in Klaviyo</h2>\n<p>Create brand voice guidelines for your account using the <em>Voice</em> tab in Klaviyo: </p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Content &gt; Images &amp; brand</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select the <strong>Voice</strong> tab. Sample brand voice content auto-generates upon page load.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/35895452729755\" alt=\"The Voice tab in Klaviyo showing auto-generated brand voice sample content.\" width=\"570\" height=\"412\">\n</li>\n<li>Review the brand voice within the sample content.\n<ol>\n<ol>\n<li>(Optional) Select <strong>Upload style guide</strong> to attach your brand’s style guide for further specifications.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Edit voice</strong> to manually adjust or add voice descriptors and writing rules.\n<ol>\n<li>From the editing modal, you can:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Click the dropdown on any voice descriptor or writing rule to edit its title or description.</li>\n<li>Use the <strong>Add</strong> button to add new voice descriptors or writing rules.</li>\n<li>Use the trash can icon to remove any descriptors or writing rules.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update Preview</strong> to see how the changes affect the sample content. Do this each time you make a change.</li>\n<li>When you’re satisfied with the brand voice in the content, click <strong>Save</strong>.<br>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</ol>\n<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>If satisfied</strong>, no further action is needed. Your brand voice guidelines will integrate automatically.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>If changes are needed</strong>:</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/35895452734491\" alt=\"The brand voice editing modal open on the Voice tab in Klaviyo.\"></p>\n<p>Going forward, when you use AI to generate email content, Klaviyo automatically applies your configured brand voice settings to the drafts that Email AI proposes for you. </p>\n<p>Note that if you haven't defined brand voice guidelines on the <em>Voice</em> page yet, clicking the brand voice icon in the email editor will also generate and automatically apply them to Email AIi content.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DS3A0XHKR66JJ5J42N\">Edit your brand voice guidelines</h2>\n<p>As your branding evolves, you can continuously update and refine your brand voice guidelines. You can make edits to brand voice guidelines in 2 places:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>During the content creation process for AI-generated email content (for quick edits)</li>\n<li>From the <em>Voice</em> settings page (for more complex edits)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DSRE7TP5TRGSZEX9VA\">Edit brand voice during content creation</h3>\n<p>While creating a campaign with Email AI, you can make quick adjustments to brand voice guidelines. To do so:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the purple brand voice icon.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/35895469298459\" alt=\"The brand voice icon highlighted on the Email AI content generation page.\" width=\"454\" height=\"421\">\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>If you haven't already established brand voice guidelines in Klaviyo's <em>Voice</em> tab, clicking this icon will generate them for your account and sync them to the <em>Voice</em> page.</p>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>In the editing modal that appears you can:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Click the dropdown on any voice descriptor or writing rule to replace or edit it.</li>\n<li>Use the trash can icon to remove any voice descriptors or writing rules.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Apply changes</strong>. </li>\n</ol>\n<p>Note that changes made here affect your entire account’s brand voice settings, not just the specific content you’re creating.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DSQVPK490C2P2P6T5G\">Edit brand voice guidelines in voice settings</h3>\n<p>For more comprehensive editing to your brand voice guidelines, use the <em>Voice</em> settings page:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Content &gt; Images &amp; brand</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select the <strong>Voice</strong> tab.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/35895452743835\" alt=\"The Voice tab selected in the menu bar of the Images and brand page in Klaviyo.\" width=\"358\" height=\"131\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Edit voice</strong> to modify or add voice descriptors and writing rules.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update preview</strong> to view how the changes affect the sample content.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/35895452734491\" alt=\"The brand voice editing modal open on the Voice page in Klaviyo.\">\n</li>\n<li>Once satisfied, click <strong>Save</strong> to preserve the brand voice changes and automatically apply them to future AI-generated email content.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JRJPK4DS3RD9BD40MCS608MN\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/28242227715227\">How to use Email AI to draft an email campaign</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/5051278887835\">How to use Klaviyo’s subject line assistant</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br>\n<br>\n<br>\n</p>",
